@parties
go-to: menu

**SPD** - *Sozialdemokratische Partei Deutschlands* (Social Democratic Party of Germany) - this is us. Germany's oldest party, rooted in the labour movement, standing for the welfare state, workers' rights and parliamentary democracy.

**CDU/CSU** - *Christlich Demokratische Union* and its Bavarian sister party, the *Christlich-Soziale Union* - the centre-right "Union". Conservative and pro-business, it leads the current government in coalition with us.

Current relations: [+ cdu_relation : relationships +]

**Grüne** - *Bündnis 90/Die Grünen* (Alliance 90/The Greens) - a centre-left party focused on climate protection, civil liberties and European integration, strongest among the urban, educated middle class.

Current relations: [+ greens_relation : relationships +]

**FDP** - *Freie Demokratische Partei* (Free Democratic Party) - a liberal, pro-market party of the self-employed and professionals. It fell out of the Bundestag in 2025.

Current relations: [+ fdp_relation : relationships +]

**Die Linke** (The Left) - a democratic socialist party to our left, critical of NATO and of the debt brake. It returned strongly in 2025, above all among young voters.

Current relations: [+ linke_relation : relationships +]

**BSW** - *Bündnis Sahra Wagenknecht* - a split from Die Linke that combines left-wing economics with conservative positions on migration and a Russia-friendly foreign policy. It narrowly missed the 5% threshold in 2025.

Current relations: [+ bsw_relation : relationships +]

[? if sapd_formed: SAPD - a party recently formed in a split from the left wing of the SPD. ?]

**AfD** - *Alternative für Deutschland* (Alternative for Germany) - a far-right, nationalist party, the largest opposition force in the Bundestag. All other parties refuse to govern with it: the "Brandmauer" (firewall).

Current relations: [+ afd_relation : relationships +]

**Other parties** - small parties below the 5% threshold, such as the Freie Wähler, Volt and the Tierschutzpartei. The SSW, the party of the Danish minority, is exempt from the threshold.

@defense
go-to: menu

**Defense and security**

**Bundeswehr**: [+ bundeswehr_strength +] thousand active soldiers. This is Germany's military.

Loyalty: [+ bundeswehr_loyalty : loyalty +]

**Verfassungsschutz**: the domestic intelligence service, which watches anti-constitutional movements.

Reliability: [+ verfassungsschutz_loyalty : loyalty +]



@factions
go-to: menu

**Internal factions of the SPD**

Overall dissent: [+ dissent_percent : dissent +]

**Parlamentarische Linke**

The Parlamentarische Linke (Parliamentary Left) and the Forum DL21 form the left wing of the party, close to the Jusos. They want redistribution, a looser debt brake and closer cooperation with the Greens and Die Linke, and they are sceptical of coalitions with the CDU/CSU.

Strength: [+ left_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ left_dissent : dissent +]

**Netzwerk Berlin**

Netzwerk Berlin is the pragmatic camp around the party leadership. Its members seek a middle course between the left and right wings of the party, and put governing and party unity first.

Strength: [+ center_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ center_dissent : dissent +]

**AfA**

The AfA (Arbeitsgemeinschaft für Arbeit) is the party's trade union wing. Many of its members also belong to the unions of the DGB. Their goal is secure jobs, higher wages and benefits for organized workers.

Strength: [+ labor_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ labor_dissent : dissent +]

**Seeheimer Kreis**

The Seeheimer Kreis is the conservative wing of the party. Its members are pragmatic participants in government, who favour fiscal discipline, a strong economy and coalitions with the parties of the centre.

Strength: [+ reformist_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ reformist_dissent : dissent +]

@figures
title: Figures and Charts
go-to: menu
on-display: {!
data = [
    {
        "id": "linke",
        "legend": "Linke",
        "name": "Linke",
        "seats": Q.linke_r*5,
    }];
if (Q.sapd_formed && Q.sapd_r) {
    data.push({
            "id": "sapd",
            "legend": "SAPD",
            "name": "SAPD",
            "seats": Q.sapd_r*5,
            });
}
data.push({
        "id": "spd",
        "legend": "SPD",
        "name": "SPD",
        "seats": Q.spd_r*5,
});

if (Q.srpd_formed && Q.srpd_r) {
    data.push({
            "id": "srpd",
            "legend": "SRPD",
            "name": "SRPD",
            "seats": Q.srpd_r*5,
            });
}

data = data.concat([
    {
        "id": "greens",
        "legend": "Grüne",
        "name": "Grüne",
        "seats": Q.greens_r*5,
    },
    {
        "id": "cdu",
        "legend": "CDU/CSU",
        "name": "CDU/CSU",
        "seats": Q.cdu_r*5,
    },
    {
        "id": "csu",
        "legend": "CSU",
        "name": "CSU",
        "seats": Q.csu_r*5,
    },
    {
        "id": "fdp",
        "legend": "FDP",
        "name": "FDP",
        "seats": Q.fdp_r*5,
    },
    {
        "id": "other",
        "legend": "Other",
        "name": "Other",
        "seats": Q.other_r*5,
    },
    {
        "id": "bsw",
        "legend": "BSW",
        "name": "BSW",
        "seats": Q.bsw_r*5,
    },
    {
        "id": "afd",
        "legend": "AfD",
        "name": "AfD",
        "seats": Q.afd_r*5,
    },
]);
if (d3 && window) {
    // get screen width
    var width = 500;
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50;
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("reichstag").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    }
    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#reichstag").datum(data).call(parliament);

    var lines = d3.linegraph(false, false,
            Q.parties,
            {'spd': '#E3000F', 'linke': '#B61C3E', 'greens': '#46962B', 'cdu': '#000000', 'csu': '#0080C9', 'fdp': '#C8A800', 'bsw': '#542344', 'afd': '#009EE0', 'ssw': '#003C8F', 'other': '#a0a0a0', 'sapd': '#c40000', 'srpd': '#F4A460'},
            {'spd': 'SPD', 'linke': 'Linke', 'greens': 'Grüne', 'cdu': 'CDU/CSU', 'csu': 'CSU', 'fdp': 'FDP', 'bsw': 'BSW', 'afd': 'AfD', 'ssw': 'SSW', 'other': 'Others', 'sapd': 'SAPD', 'srpd': 'SRPD'});
    lines.width(width).height(400);
    //var svg = lines(Q.election_records);
    if (Q.election_records.length > 0) {
        d3.select("#election_history").datum(Q.election_records).call(lines);
    }
    //document.getElementById('election_history').innerHTML = svg.outerHTML;

    // party support records should not have so many ticks
    if (!Q.historical_mode || Q.game_over) {
        var lines_2 = d3.linegraph(true, true,
            Q.parties,
            {'spd': '#E3000F', 'linke': '#B61C3E', 'greens': '#46962B', 'cdu': '#000000', 'csu': '#0080C9', 'fdp': '#C8A800', 'bsw': '#542344', 'afd': '#009EE0', 'ssw': '#003C8F', 'other': '#a0a0a0', 'sapd': '#c40000', 'srpd': '#F4A460'},
            {'spd': 'SPD', 'linke': 'Linke', 'greens': 'Grüne', 'cdu': 'CDU/CSU', 'csu': 'CSU', 'fdp': 'FDP', 'bsw': 'BSW', 'afd': 'AfD', 'ssw': 'SSW', 'other': 'Others', 'sapd': 'SAPD', 'srpd': 'SRPD'});
        lines_2.width(width).height(400);
        d3.select("#party_support_history").datum(Q.party_support_records).call(lines_2);
    }

    // economic stats
    var minInflation = d3.min(Q.economic_records, d => d.inflation);
    var maxUnemployment = d3.max(Q.economic_records, d => d.unemployment);
    var lines_3 = d3.linegraph(true, true, ['inflation', 'unemployment'],
            {'inflation': '#0000FF', 'unemployment': '#FF0000'},
            {'inflation': 'Inflation', 'unemployment': 'Unemployment'},
            maxUnemployment + 5, minInflation - 5, 21);
    lines_3.width(width).height(300);
    d3.select("#economic_history").datum(Q.economic_records).call(lines_3);
}
!}

